exports[`autoprune (J1 — the clamp that bites) given: [case4] what a real run WRITES TO STDERR, end to end when: [t1] the same run, with the hold hatch ON then: 🔴 the hold message REACHES a human, whole and unaltered 1`] = `
"🧹 test-fns: TEST_FNS_KEEP is set, so this run KEPT ALL of its temp dirs.
   ├─ at: <tmpDir>
   ├─ run: <run>
   ├─ scope: every dir this run made — a green run holds them too, since a
   │         global teardown is handed no test results to filter by.
   ├─ they are reclaimed by the age gate after 86400000ms (24h) — widen
   │  that window with TEST_FNS_MAX_AGE_MS, in ms.
   └─ done with them? remove this run's, and no peer's:
        rm -rf "<tmpDir>"/*.<run>.*

"
`;

exports[`autoprune (J1 — the clamp that bites) given: [case5] an UNHOOKED consumer — every repo on release day when: [t0] the runner config wires neither hook then: 🔴 the notice REACHES a human, whole and unaltered 1`] = `
"🧹 test-fns: temp dirs made by genTempDir are never reclaimed here.
   ├─ at: your jest config (this repo may hold several)
   ├─ cause: this runner config does not wire the autoprune hooks.
   ├─ fix (jest): add both keys —
   │      globalSetup: 'test-fns/autoprune.setup.jest'
   │      globalTeardown: 'test-fns/autoprune.teardown.jest'
   ├─ fix (vitest): add the one key —
   │      globalSetup: ['test-fns/autoprune.setup.vitest']
   └─ quiet: set TEST_FNS_QUIET=1

"
`;

