exports[`autoprune (J1 — the clamp that bites) given: [case7] a run PRE-EMPTED, then the next run starts when: [t0] the next run speaks its arrears to a real terminal then: and what a human reads is shaped as here 1`] = `
"🧹 test-fns: 1 prior test run never reclaimed its temp dirs.
   ├─ run: <runA> — pid <pid> (gone), began <ts>
   │  ├─ 1 temp dir still on disk with its stamp
   │  └─ its teardown never ran
   ├─ cause: a class of pre-emption — a signal, a CI hard timeout, an OOM, or
   │         a throw inside the global setup or teardown. it got no second write.
   └─ fix: no fix is owed if you interrupted that run on purpose. if it ended
           on its own, check the runner logs at that timestamp — the residue
           itself is bounded by the age gate.

"
`;

